From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:07:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sep: let a boot policy change update its xART
 record

A new Stage 1 changes the boot policy the Mac keeps for Linux. The first
time Linux's identity keybag is unlocked under the new policy, the
enclave rewrites one session record that already existed. Linux did not
create it, so the xART guard refuses the write. The enclave then never
answers CHANGE_LOCK_STATE, the machine ref-key stays down and every
trusted-key seal fails with EIO, so Touch ID is gone until the policy
changes back. On a J616s (T6040) this happened after a Stage 1 reinstall
that changed only the kernel collection hash.

Under an unchanged policy that first unlock rewrites no session record at
all, so a rewrite inside it is the policy change. Let exactly one through:
during the first unlock of an identity keybag that already existed, once
per boot, one kind-4 session record, a rewrite and never a delete, and
only once the record's previous value is durable in a host file. The
record is not added to Linux's list. A ref-key created this boot closes
the window.

For a change the window does not cover, aurora-sep-policy-change leaves a
one-time allowance in /var/lib/aurora-sep-xart-allow-once.bin naming the
refused record, or before a planned change the first existing kind-4
record asked for. The driver empties the file at probe before it uses
it, so an allowance lasts one boot, on the same terms.

Name refused records by their session id. Linux's list of records
already holds session ids, so this reveals nothing new.

On the J616s the allowance restored Touch ID with the existing enrolment:
one kind-4 record and one shared root were rewritten, the other seven
session records kept their revisions, and the enrolled finger matched.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e89d4a291bee99e48ab4433bc1c2656c7d8641ae)

